{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"574338ed-c703-4be9-aa75-9325d2641fc9","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The issue has been identified and fixed. Details have been documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-nI0nyD/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Cause \u0026 Fix\n\n- **Cause**: Even when configured with OpenRouter, Mistral Vibe attempts to resolve `MISTRAL_API_KEY` at startup before anything else. Because [run-vibe.sh](file:///tmp/h-nI0nyD/run-vibe.sh) runs Vibe via `env -i` without passing `MISTRAL_API_KEY`, Vibe fell back to looking for keys in the macOS Keychain via `/usr/bin/security`. [agent.sb](file:///tmp/h-nI0nyD/agent.sb) explicitly denies `/usr/bin/security`, causing Vibe to crash immediately with exit code 2 (`[Errno 1] Operation not permitted: '/usr/bin/security'`).\n- **Fix**: Added `MISTRAL_API_KEY=unused` to the `env -i` command invocation in [run-vibe.sh](file:///tmp/h-nI0nyD/run-vibe.sh). This prevents Vibe from invoking `/usr/bin/security` while keeping the sandbox strictly enforced.\n","duration_seconds":68.495461,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":192324,"output_tokens":2030,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":74882,"total_tokens":194354}}}
